given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Breitling</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Increased prevalence of intestinal helminth infection during pregnancy in a Sub-Saharan African community.</article-title><source>Wien Klin Wochenschr</source><volume>119</volume><fpage>712</fpage><lpage>716</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18157604</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000473-Herter1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Herter</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Petney</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Pipitgool</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Sithithaworn</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Vivatpatanakul</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>The influence of pregnancy on intestinal parasite infection in Thai women.</article-title><source>Acta Tropica</source><volume>101</volume><fpage>200</fpage><lpage>206</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17349963</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000473-Shulman1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shulman</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>Dorman</surname><given-names>EK</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Reducing childhood mortality in poor countries: Importance and prevention of malaria in pregnancy.</article-title><source>Trans R Soc Trop Med Hyg</source><volume>97</volume><fpage>30</fpage><lpage>35</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12886801</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pntd.0000473-Schmid1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schmid</surname><given-names>GP</given-names></name><name><surname>Stoner</surname><given-names>